<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
                           xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                           revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0"
                           xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Claude Desktop</displayName>
  <description>Enterprise policy settings for Claude Desktop for Windows (HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude).</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>

      <!-- Supported on -->
      <string id="SUPPORTED_ClaudeDesktop">Claude Desktop for Windows</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_ClaudeDesktop_1_25927">Claude Desktop for Windows 1.25927.0 or later</string>

      <!-- Categories -->
      <string id="Cat_Anthropic">Anthropic</string>
      <string id="Cat_ClaudeDesktop">Claude Desktop</string>
      <string id="Cat_SignIn">Sign-in</string>
      <string id="Cat_Updates">Updates</string>
      <string id="Cat_ClaudeCode">Claude Code</string>
      <string id="Cat_Cowork">Cowork</string>
      <string id="Cat_Extensions">Extensions and MCP</string>

      <!-- Sign-in -->
      <string id="ForceLoginOrgUUID">Restrict sign-in to specific organization(s)</string>
      <string id="ForceLoginOrgUUID_Help">Requires users to sign in to Claude Desktop with an account that belongs to one of the specified Claude organizations. Sign-in fails if the account is not a member of a listed organization.

Registry: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\forceLoginOrgUUID (REG_SZ)

Value formats:
  - A single organization UUID, e.g.  11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555
    A single UUID also pre-selects that organization at sign-in.
  - A JSON array of UUIDs, e.g.  ["uuid-1","uuid-2"]
    Any listed organization is accepted; none is pre-selected.

Claude Desktop reads this value at launch. Users must quit and reopen the app after a change.

If you enable this policy, sign-in is restricted to the organization(s) entered.
If you disable or do not configure this policy, users can sign in with any account.</string>

      <!-- Updates -->
      <string id="DisableAutoUpdates">Disable automatic updates</string>
      <string id="DisableAutoUpdates_Help">Turns off Claude Desktop's built-in automatic updates.

Enable this when your MDM (for example Intune) manages Claude Desktop versions. Leave it not configured to let the app update itself after a one-time provisioned install.

Registry: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\disableAutoUpdates (REG_DWORD)
  Enabled = 1 (automatic updates off)
  Disabled = 0 (automatic updates on)
  Not configured = value removed (default: automatic updates on)</string>

      <string id="AutoUpdaterEnforcementHours">Update enforcement window (hours)</string>
      <string id="AutoUpdaterEnforcementHours_Help">Sets how many hours Claude Desktop waits before it forcibly restarts to apply an update that has already been downloaded and prepared.

Valid range: 1-72. Default when not configured: 72.

Registry: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\autoUpdaterEnforcementHours (REG_DWORD)

This setting has no effect if automatic updates are disabled.</string>

      <!-- Claude Code -->
      <string id="IsClaudeCodeForDesktopEnabled">Allow Claude Code in Claude Desktop</string>
      <string id="IsClaudeCodeForDesktopEnabled_Help">Controls whether users can access Claude Code inside the Claude Desktop app.

Registry: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\isClaudeCodeForDesktopEnabled (REG_DWORD)
  Enabled = 1 (Claude Code available)
  Disabled = 0 (Claude Code blocked)
  Not configured = app default (available)</string>

      <string id="EffortLevel">Default effort level for Claude Code sessions</string>
      <string id="EffortLevel_Help">Sets the default effort level for Claude Code sessions in Claude Desktop. The value is applied at the start of every session, even if the user changed it in an earlier session.

Does not apply to Cowork sessions. Requires Claude Desktop 1.25927.0 or later.

Registry: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\effortLevel (REG_SZ)
  Allowed values: low, medium, high, xhigh, max

If you disable or do not configure this policy, the app's normal default is used.</string>
      <string id="EffortLevel_Low">Low</string>
      <string id="EffortLevel_Medium">Medium</string>
      <string id="EffortLevel_High">High</string>
      <string id="EffortLevel_XHigh">Extra high (xhigh)</string>
      <string id="EffortLevel_Max">Max</string>

      <!-- Cowork -->
      <string id="SecureVmFeaturesEnabled">Allow Cowork in Claude Desktop</string>
      <string id="SecureVmFeaturesEnabled_Help">Controls whether users can access Cowork (the secure VM workspace) in the Claude Desktop app.

Registry: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\secureVmFeaturesEnabled (REG_DWORD)
  Enabled = 1 (Cowork available)
  Disabled = 0 (Cowork blocked)
  Not configured = app default (available)</string>

      <string id="AllowedWorkspaceFolders">Restrict folders that can be mounted in Cowork</string>
      <string id="AllowedWorkspaceFolders_Help">Limits which file-system paths users can mount into Cowork.

Enter a JSON array of folder paths. Backslashes must be escaped (doubled) because the value is JSON, for example:
  ["C:\\Users\\Public\\Projects","D:\\Shared\\Claude"]

Registry: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\allowedWorkspaceFolders (REG_SZ, JSON text)

If you disable or do not configure this policy, users can mount any folder.

Enterprise plans can also set this in Organization settings on claude.ai.</string>

      <string id="CoworkEDRIntegration">Cowork EDR sensor integration (beta)</string>
      <string id="CoworkEDRIntegration_Help">Installs your endpoint detection and response (EDR) vendor's signed sensor package inside the Cowork environment.

  Vendor ID: your EDR vendor's identifier, in lowercase.
  Sensor package path: the full path to the vendor's signed sensor package on the user's computer.

Registry (both REG_SZ):
  HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\coworkEDRIntegrationVendor
  HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\coworkEDRIntegration

If you disable or do not configure this policy, no EDR package is installed.
This is a beta feature; confirm supported vendor IDs with Anthropic before deploying.</string>

      <!-- Extensions & MCP -->
      <string id="IsDesktopExtensionEnabled">Allow desktop extensions</string>
      <string id="IsDesktopExtensionEnabled_Help">Controls whether users can install and use desktop extensions in Claude Desktop.

Registry: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\isDesktopExtensionEnabled (REG_DWORD)
  Enabled = 1, Disabled = 0, Not configured = app default (allowed)

Note: Do not disable this policy if you want to use the in-app extension allowlist; machine-level policy overrides the allowlist.</string>

      <string id="IsDesktopExtensionDirectoryEnabled">Allow the extension directory</string>
      <string id="IsDesktopExtensionDirectoryEnabled_Help">Controls whether users can browse and install from the Claude Desktop extension directory.

Registry: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\isDesktopExtensionDirectoryEnabled (REG_DWORD)
  Enabled = 1, Disabled = 0, Not configured = app default (allowed)

Note: Do not disable this policy if you want to use the in-app extension allowlist; machine-level policy overrides the allowlist.</string>

      <string id="IsLocalDevMcpEnabled">Allow local MCP servers</string>
      <string id="IsLocalDevMcpEnabled_Help">Controls whether users can configure and run local (developer) MCP servers in Claude Desktop.

Registry: HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude\isLocalDevMcpEnabled (REG_DWORD)
  Enabled = 1, Disabled = 0, Not configured = app default (allowed)</string>

    </stringTable>

    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="ForceLoginOrgUUID">
        <textBox refId="ForceLoginOrgUUID_Value">
          <label>Organization UUID, or JSON array of UUIDs:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>

      <presentation id="AutoUpdaterEnforcementHours">
        <decimalTextBox refId="AutoUpdaterEnforcementHours_Value" defaultValue="72" spinStep="1">Hours before forced restart (1-72):</decimalTextBox>
      </presentation>

      <presentation id="EffortLevel">
        <dropdownList refId="EffortLevel_Value" noSort="true" defaultItem="2">Default effort level:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>

      <presentation id="AllowedWorkspaceFolders">
        <textBox refId="AllowedWorkspaceFolders_Value">
          <label>Allowed folders (JSON array, backslashes doubled):</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>

      <presentation id="CoworkEDRIntegration">
        <textBox refId="CoworkEDRIntegrationVendor_Value">
          <label>EDR vendor ID (lowercase):</label>
        </textBox>
        <textBox refId="CoworkEDRIntegration_Value">
          <label>Full path to signed sensor package:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
